# Hawaii 2026 Agent Guardrails

- Treat `src/` as source of truth; treat `_site/` as generated output.
- Prefer editing files under `src/` unless user explicitly requests a direct `_site/` patch.
- If `_site/` is edited for a quick fix, mirror the same change in `src/` when possible.
- Preserve existing project style and naming conventions in Nunjucks, CSS, and JS.
- Reuse existing partials/layouts in `src/_includes/` before adding new structure.
- Do not add new dependencies unless clearly required.
- Keep accessibility intact: meaningful `alt` text, ARIA only when needed, semantic headings.
- For visual fixes, check shared styles in `src/css/components.css` before page-specific overrides.
- Avoid destructive actions (delete/reset/force) unless explicitly requested.
